INDEX(7)                    MiniOS Manual

NAME
    index - terminal userland manual index

DESCRIPTION
    Run man with no arguments to list installed manual pages. man name
    displays a page, man -k keyword searches descriptions, man -f name
    prints a summary and man -w name prints its installed path.

    Shell:       sh, alias, echo, read, test
    Files:       ls, tree, df, find, mount, fsinit, fstab(5)
    Text:        cat, grep, sed, awk, head, tail, less, pager, xargs, gzip
    Processes:   ps
    Build:       make, ar
    Archives:    tar, gzip
    Help:        man, index

    Interactive shells read /etc/profile and $HOME/.shrc. The console and
    Terminal window provide history, completion and cursor editing.
    Colour output is disabled for pipes and when NO_COLOR is set or TERM
    is absent or dumb. Set PAGER or MANPAGER to choose a manual viewer.
